  "constraints": {
    "notes": "Bounded contiguous FP32 caller buffers; rows and channels are positive signed-int bounds. Outputs must not alias. Training emitter validates all map spans before generating a call. Epsilon is an operation-local positive FP32 literal. Finite operands are a caller precondition; this legacy void provider does not promise atomic rejection of nonfinite data."
  },
  "notes": "Reuses existing native arithmetic. Forward caches the actual FP32 mean/rstd. Backward consumes these statistics, overwrites d_input, and accumulates d_gamma/d_beta into zeroed temporary gradient buffers; graph accumulation owns shared-parameter sums. Not BF16 or complete Clef training. Forward uses the existing GGML-matched sum/variance reductions: FP32 SIMD partials, FP64 sum of partials, FP32 mean/variance/rstd caches and affine stores. SIMD chunk width is compile-target dependent.",
